I={
"Estimating & Takeoff":("Takeoff and estimating tools turn plans into quantities and quantities into a price. Newer AI takeoff tools try to count and measure from PDFs automatically, while older desktop tools rely on you clicking areas and runs.",["Which drawing formats it reads (PDF, CAD, scanned sets)","Whether takeoff feeds straight into an estimate or proposal","Trade fit: general, roofing, electrical, landscaping or paving"]),
"Bidding & Preconstruction":("Preconstruction tools help you find projects, send bid invitations, and review contracts before you commit. Some are networks, some are AI assistants that read documents for risk.",["Whether the bid network covers your region and project size","How subcontractor invites and responses are tracked","Whether AI document review explains why a clause was flagged"]),
"Project Management & Scheduling":("Construction project management software keeps schedules, budgets, change orders, and client communication in one place. Residential builders and commercial GCs usually need different depth.",["Residential vs. commercial focus","Client portal and change-order approvals","Mobile app quality for crews in the field"]),
"Field Service, CRM & Invoicing":("Field service tools run the day-to-day of a trades business: quotes, dispatch, scheduling, invoicing, and getting paid. Roofing and HVAC have specialized options, and a newer group uses AI to answer calls or coach sales reps.",["Quote-to-invoice flow and online payments","Dispatch and scheduling for multiple techs","Integrations with your accounting software"]),
"Drawings, Photos & Documentation":("Documentation tools capture what was built and when: jobsite photos, 360 walkthroughs, drone maps, aerial roof measurements, and floor plans from a phone.",["How photos and scans are organized by job","Whether measurements are accurate enough to order materials","Sharing with clients, adjusters and subs"]),
"Safety, Time & Compliance":("Safety and time tools cover inspections, toolbox talks, daily reports, and GPS timesheets. Good records here protect you on payroll disputes and incident claims.",["Offline use on sites without signal","GPS or geofenced clock-in options","Report exports for OSHA, owners and insurers"]),
"Accounting, Payroll & Payments":("Contractor finances have quirks general accounting doesn't: job costing, retainage, pay applications, and certified payroll. These tools range from general small-business accounting to construction-specific billing.",["Job costing and retainage support","Pay application (AIA-style) billing","Payroll that handles multiple job sites and states"]),
"AI Assistants for Contractors":("General AI assistants can draft bid emails, scopes of work, safety talks, and client updates. Treat their output as a first draft and check numbers, code requirements, and contract terms yourself.",["Data privacy for client and bid information","Whether it can read your PDFs and photos","Cost per seat for a small crew"]),
"Tip & Bill Split":("Tip calculators handle a single check; bill-splitting apps track who owes what across a trip or a shared household. Pick by whether you need a quick number or a running balance.",["One-off calculation vs. ongoing group balances","Works offline or without an account","Handles uneven splits and tax/tip on top"]),
"Mortgage & Housing":("Mortgage calculators estimate a monthly payment from price, down payment, rate, and term. The better ones include property tax, insurance, PMI, and an amortization schedule.",["Includes taxes, insurance and PMI","Shows an amortization schedule","Uses your own rate rather than a sponsored one"]),
"Tax & Paycheck":("Paycheck calculators estimate take-home pay after withholding; filing tools prepare the return. Official IRS tools are the reference point for withholding.",["Up to date for the current tax year","State and local tax coverage","Free tier limits and upsells during filing"]),
"Budgeting":("Budgeting apps range from zero-based (give every dollar a job) to automatic spending trackers. Open-source and self-hosted options keep your data on your own device.",["Method: zero-based, envelopes, or tracking","Bank sync vs. manual entry","Subscription price and data ownership"]),
"Currency & FX":("Currency converters show exchange rates; the rate you actually pay at a bank or card network is usually different. Mid-market and central-bank reference rates are useful baselines.",["Mid-market vs. retail rate","How often rates update","Historical charts if you need them"]),
"Savings, Debt & Retirement":("These calculators model compound growth, debt payoff order, and whether a retirement plan survives historical markets. They are planning aids, not advice.",["Snowball vs. avalanche debt options","Historical or Monte Carlo retirement modeling","Inflation and fee assumptions you can change"]),
"Credit & Banking":("Official consumer tools for checking credit reports, confirming a bank is insured, and filing complaints.",["Official source (government or federally authorized)","No paid upsell to see your own report","Clear complaint or dispute steps"]),
"General Calculators":("General-purpose calculators for math, graphing, and quick conversions that come up in money questions.",["Shows the formula or steps","Works on mobile","No account needed"]),
"Agent platforms":("No-code and low-code agent platforms let you connect an LLM to apps, data, and triggers without writing a full application. Open-source options can be self-hosted.",["Self-hosting vs. cloud only","Number and depth of app integrations","Human-in-the-loop approval steps"]),
"Voice agents":("Voice agent platforms answer and place phone calls with an AI agent: speech recognition, a language model, and text-to-speech joined with low latency.",["Latency and interruption handling","Telephony numbers and call transfer","Per-minute pricing and compliance features"]),
"Frameworks & SDKs":("Agent frameworks give developers building blocks: tool calling, memory, multi-agent orchestration, and tracing. Choice is often driven by language (Python vs. TypeScript) and how much control you want.",["Python or TypeScript","Stateful orchestration and retries","Model-provider neutrality"]),
"Coding agents":("Coding agents read a codebase, edit files, run commands, and open pull requests. Some live in an editor, some in the terminal, and some build whole apps from a prompt.",["Editor, terminal, or browser-based","Can it run tests and iterate on failures","Repo and secret access controls"]),
"Browser & computer-use agents":("Browser agents and infrastructure let an AI navigate websites: hosted headless browsers, open-source agent libraries, and MCP servers that expose browser control.",["Hosted vs. self-run browsers","Session recording and debugging","Respecting site terms and logins"]),
"Observability & evals":("Observability and evaluation tools trace each LLM call and tool step, score outputs, and catch regressions before users do.",["Open-source or self-hostable","Tracing for multi-step agents","Datasets and automated evals"]),
"Protocols & use-case guides":("Open protocols and reference guides for connecting agents to tools and to each other, plus design patterns from model providers.",["Open specification and governance","Reference implementations","Practical examples you can copy"]),
}
